      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) If the System Operator is required to cancel the registration of the healthcare recipient under subsection 51(1);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the System Operator must destroy any record that includes health information that is included in the My Health Record of the healthcare recipient, other than..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-6-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(4) At the end of section 17",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-6-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The System Operator must comply with subsection (3):\n\n(a) as soon as practicable after the cancellation decision takes\neffect under subsection 51(7); or\n\n(b) if any of the following requirements apply before the records\nare destroyed under paragraph (a)—as soon as practicable\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\n\nafter the conclusion of the matter to which the requirement\nrelates:\n\n(i) a court order requires the System Operator not to\ndestroy records of the healthcare recipient;\n\n(ii) the System Operator is required to disclose records of\nthe healthcare recipient under section 69 or 69A;\n\n(iii) the System Operator is required to disclose records of\nthe healthcare recipient under a law covered by\nsubsection 65(3).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The System Operator must comply with subsection (3):\n\n(a) as soon as practicable after the cancellation decision takes\neffect under subsection 51(7); or\n\n(b) if any of the following requirements apply before the records\nare destroyed under paragraph (a)—as soon as practicable\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\n\nafter the conclusion of the matter to which the requirement\nrelates:\n\n(i) a court order requires the System Operator not to\ndestroy records of the healthcare recipient;\n\n(ii) the System Operator is required to disclose records of\nthe healthcare recipient under section 69 or 69A;\n\n(iii) the System Operator is required to disclose records of\nthe healthcare recipient under a law covered by\nsubsection 65(3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-6-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-6-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20e48ee5da68d95703c9acab97bec0fd8a538afdfa73caf04f89ebe4a8de75c6",
      "skos:note": "Comply with subsection (3) after cancellation decision takes effect or if certain requirements apply before records are destroyed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-6-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(4) At the end of section 17",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The System Operator must comply with subsection (3):\n\n(a) as soon as practicable after the cancellation decision takes\neffect under subsection 51(7); or\n\n(b) if any of the following requirements apply before the records\nare destroyed under paragraph (a)—as soon as practicable\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\n\nafter the conclusion of the matter to which the requirement\nrelates:\n\n(i) a court order requires the System Operator not to\ndestroy records of the healthcare recipient;\n\n(ii) the System Operator is required to disclose records of\nthe healthcare recipient under section 69 or 69A;\n\n(iii) the System Operator is required to disclose records of\nthe healthcare recipient under a law covered by\nsubsection 65(3)."
    },
