    {
      "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59A Unauthorised use of information included in a healthcare",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-59a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "recipient’s My Health Record for prohibited purpose\n\n(1) A person must not use health information included in a healthcare\nrecipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited purpose, if the\nperson obtained the information by using or gaining access to the\nMy Health Record system.\nNote:\nFor prohibited purpose, see section 70A.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person is the healthcare\nrecipient, but does apply if the person is the nominated\nrepresentative of the healthcare recipient (despite subsection 7(2)).",
      "skos:definition": "recipient’s My Health Record for prohibited purpose\n\n(1) A person must not use health information included in a healthcare\nrecipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited purpose, if the\nperson obtained the information by using or gaining access to the\nMy Health Record system.\nNote:\nFor prohibited purpose, see section 70A.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person is the healthcare\nrecipient, but does apply if the person is the nominated\nrepresentative of the healthcare recipient (despite subsection 7(2)).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc096c3d303d7a9e473439189854c4fa76daab5a7ae5490760a1d940b9323b36"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-59a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59A Unauthorised use of information included in a healthcare",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "recipient’s My Health Record for prohibited purpose\n\n(1) A person must not use health information included in a healthcare\nrecipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited purpose, if the\nperson obtained the information by using or gaining access to the\nMy Health Record system.\nNote:\nFor prohibited purpose, see section 70A.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person is the healthcare\nrecipient, but does apply if the person is the nominated\nrepresentative of the healthcare recipient (despite subsection 7(2))."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59A(1) Unauthorised use of information included in a healthcare",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-59a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not use health information included in a healthcare\nrecipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited purpose, if the\nperson obtained the information by using or gaining access to the\nMy Health Record system.\nNote:\nFor prohibited purpose, see section 70A.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person must not use health information included in a healthcare\nrecipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited purpose, if the\nperson obtained the information by using or gaining access to the\nMy Health Record system.\nNote:\nFor prohibited purpose, see section 70A.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-59a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "79f63be555874144ede69cbac78fca50274bd8d7590e113fe1e421086a0bf3bd",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on using health information for a prohibited purpose."
    },
    {
