    {
      "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "69A(5) Disclosure to designated entity under order by judicial officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-69a-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A designated entity may apply to any of the following judicial\nofficers:\n\n(a) a magistrate of a State or Territory;\n\n(b) a judge who is eligible under subsection 69B(2);\nfor an order under this section in relation to the disclosure, to the\nentity, of health information included in a healthcare recipient’s\nMy Health Record.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A designated entity may apply to any of the following judicial\nofficers:\n\n(a) a magistrate of a State or Territory;\n\n(b) a judge who is eligible under subsection 69B(2);\nfor an order under this section in relation to the disclosure, to the\nentity, of health information included in a healthcare recipient’s\nMy Health Record.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a"
      },
