        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a-ss-5-logic-ltl-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a-ss-5-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-69a-ss-5-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "119a6050f5ec9b410ac15f0eac47ace67300f4b96a7b2a6dba8192adeef99321",
      "skos:note": "Application for order under section 69A(5)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-69a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "69A(5) Disclosure to designated entity under order by judicial officer",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(5) A designated entity may apply to any of the following judicial\nofficers:\n\n(a) a magistrate of a State or Territory;\n\n(b) a judge who is eligible under subsection 69B(2);\nfor an order under this section in relation to the disclosure, to the\nentity, of health information included in a healthcare recipient’s\nMy Health Record.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018"
    },
