    {
      "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-71b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "71B Civil penalty for use of My Health Record-derived information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-71b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "for prohibited purpose\n\n(1) A person must not use health information that is or was included in\na healthcare recipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited\npurpose.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the information was not collected\nfrom, and is not derived from a disclosure that was made by, a\nperson who obtained the information by using or gaining access to\nthe My Health Record system. For this purpose, it does not matter\nwhether or not any collection or disclosure of the information was\nauthorised under this Act or any other law.\nNote:\nA person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2): see section 96 of the Regulatory Powers (Standard\nProvisions) Act 2014.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person is the healthcare\nrecipient, but does apply if the person is the nominated\nrepresentative of the healthcare recipient (despite subsection 7(2)).",
      "skos:definition": "for prohibited purpose\n\n(1) A person must not use health information that is or was included in\na healthcare recipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited\npurpose.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the information was not collected\nfrom, and is not derived from a disclosure that was made by, a\nperson who obtained the information by using or gaining access to\nthe My Health Record system. For this purpose, it does not matter\nwhether or not any collection or disclosure of the information was\nauthorised under this Act or any other law.\nNote:\nA person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2): see section 96 of the Regulatory Powers (Standard\nProvisions) Act 2014.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person is the healthcare\nrecipient, but does apply if the person is the nominated\nrepresentative of the healthcare recipient (despite subsection 7(2)).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-71b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-71b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-71b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6cb61bfe4b41596b9a6d9e2954bf93a96650adf8dc220c9650ead0f26e87b36b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-71b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "71B Civil penalty for use of My Health Record-derived information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "for prohibited purpose\n\n(1) A person must not use health information that is or was included in\na healthcare recipient’s My Health Record for a prohibited\npurpose.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the information was not collected\nfrom, and is not derived from a disclosure that was made by, a\nperson who obtained the information by using or gaining access to\nthe My Health Record system. For this purpose, it does not matter\nwhether or not any collection or disclosure of the information was\nauthorised under this Act or any other law.\nNote:\nA person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2): see section 96 of the Regulatory Powers (Standard\nProvisions) Act 2014.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person is the healthcare\nrecipient, but does apply if the person is the nominated\nrepresentative of the healthcare recipient (despite subsection 7(2))."
    },
