        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of section 17 of the My Health Records Act 2012\nmade by this Schedule apply in relation to a cancellation of registration\nof a healthcare recipient on request, whether the cancellation takes\neffect before or after the commencement of this Schedule.\n(2)\nHowever, the amendments do not apply in relation to a cancellation that\ntook effect before the commencement of this Schedule if, after the\ncancellation took effect and before the commencement of this Schedule,\nthe healthcare recipient applied for registration.\n(3)\nThe amendments made by items 6C, 16A and 16B of this Schedule\napply in relation to the use of information after this Schedule\ncommences, regardless of whether the information was collected before\nor after that commencement.\nMy Health Records (National Application) Rules 2017",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments of section 17 of the My Health Records Act 2012\nmade by this Schedule apply in relation to a cancellation of registration\nof a healthcare recipient on request, whether the cancellation takes\neffect before or after the commencement of this Schedule.\n(2)\nHowever, the amendments do not apply in relation to a cancellation that\ntook effect before the commencement of this Schedule if, after the\ncancellation took effect and before the commencement of this Schedule,\nthe healthcare recipient applied for registration.\n(3)\nThe amendments made by items 6C, 16A and 16B of this Schedule\napply in relation to the use of information after this Schedule\ncommences, regardless of whether the information was collected before\nor after that commencement.\nMy Health Records (National Application) Rules 2017",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-1-sec-17-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "16c036d154d4159c4647485f5fa843fcae3878a266e6e159204c2958b1767275",
      "skos:note": "Application of amendments to cancellation of registration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-1-sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Application of amendments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments of section 17 of the My Health Records Act 2012\nmade by this Schedule apply in relation to a cancellation of registration\nof a healthcare recipient on request, whether the cancellation takes\neffect before or after the commencement of this Schedule.\n(2)\nHowever, the amendments do not apply in relation to a cancellation that\ntook effect before the commencement of this Schedule if, after the\ncancellation took effect and before the commencement of this Schedule,\nthe healthcare recipient applied for registration.\n(3)\nThe amendments made by items 6C, 16A and 16B of this Schedule\napply in relation to the use of information after this Schedule\ncommences, regardless of whether the information was collected before\nor after that commencement.\nMy Health Records (National Application) Rules 2017"
    },
