    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-77a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "77A(1) Enforceable requirements in My Health Records Rules must",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An entity commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the entity does an act or omits to do an act; and\n\n(b) the result is that the entity contravenes a requirement\nimposed on the entity by My Health Records Rules made for\nthe purposes of subsection 109(7A) and the entity is reckless\nas to that result; and\n\nAmendments commencing on Proclamation  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\n\n(c) the My Health Records Rules provide that the requirement is\nenforceable for the purposes of this paragraph; and\n\n(d) the entity is not the System Operator, the Data Governance\nBoard established by section 82 or the data custodian.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units."
    },
