      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of a member of the\nData Governance Board if:\n\n(a) the member:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with the member’s creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of the member’s remuneration for\nthe benefit of the member’s creditors; or\n\n(b) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, from 3\nconsecutive meetings of the Board; or\n\n(c) the member engages in paid work (within the meaning of\nsection 93) that, in the Minister’s opinion, conflicts or could\nconflict with the proper performance of the member’s duties\n(see section 93); or\n\n(d) the member fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with the duty to\ndisclose interests) or rules made for the purposes of that\nsection.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of a member of the\nData Governance Board if:\n\n(a) the member:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with the member’s creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of the member’s remuneration for\nthe benefit of the member’s creditors; or\n\n(b) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, from 3\nconsecutive meetings of the Board; or\n\n(c) the member engages in paid work (within the meaning of\nsection 93) that, in the Minister’s opinion, conflicts or could\nconflict with the proper performance of the member’s duties\n(see section 93); or\n\n(d) the member fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with the duty to\ndisclose interests) or rules made for the purposes of that\nsection.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-91"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-91-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-91-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "875d451f77dbdc39f30bd3b39bf1303d6ec396f4bf67d6a2bd0132d8537c3c7d",
      "skos:note": "Termination of appointment under specified conditions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-91-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "91(2) Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of a member of the\nData Governance Board if:\n\n(a) the member:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with the member’s creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of the member’s remuneration for\nthe benefit of the member’s creditors; or\n\n(b) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, from 3\nconsecutive meetings of the Board; or\n\n(c) the member engages in paid work (within the meaning of\nsection 93) that, in the Minister’s opinion, conflicts or could\nconflict with the proper performance of the member’s duties\n(see section 93); or\n\n(d) the member fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with the duty to\ndisclose interests) or rules made for the purposes of that\nsection."
    },
