    {
      "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "96 Quorum",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-96"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) At a meeting of the Data Governance Board, a quorum is\nconstituted by a majority of members of the Board.\n\n(2) However, if:\n\n(a) a member of the Board is required by rules made for the\npurposes of section 29 of the Public Governance,\n\nAmendments commencing on Proclamation  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\n\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 not to be present\nduring the deliberations, or to take part in any decision, of the\nBoard with respect to a particular matter; and\n\n(b) when the member leaves the meeting concerned there is no\nlonger a quorum present;\nthe remaining members at the meeting constitute a quorum for the\npurpose of any deliberation or decision at that meeting with respect\nto that matter.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) At a meeting of the Data Governance Board, a quorum is\nconstituted by a majority of members of the Board.\n\n(2) However, if:\n\n(a) a member of the Board is required by rules made for the\npurposes of section 29 of the Public Governance,\n\nAmendments commencing on Proclamation  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\n\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 not to be present\nduring the deliberations, or to take part in any decision, of the\nBoard with respect to a particular matter; and\n\n(b) when the member leaves the meeting concerned there is no\nlonger a quorum present;\nthe remaining members at the meeting constitute a quorum for the\npurpose of any deliberation or decision at that meeting with respect\nto that matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7723475591f9f5df7e3538452263328226ca6a4fc4e1754022447fbddc12a63f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-96",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "96 Quorum",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1) At a meeting of the Data Governance Board, a quorum is\nconstituted by a majority of members of the Board.\n\n(2) However, if:\n\n(a) a member of the Board is required by rules made for the\npurposes of section 29 of the Public Governance,\n\nAmendments commencing on Proclamation  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\n\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013 not to be present\nduring the deliberations, or to take part in any decision, of the\nBoard with respect to a particular matter; and\n\n(b) when the member leaves the meeting concerned there is no\nlonger a quorum present;\nthe remaining members at the meeting constitute a quorum for the\npurpose of any deliberation or decision at that meeting with respect\nto that matter."
    },
