    {
      "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "96E Relationship between System Operator and Data Governance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-96e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "Board in relation to data for research or public health\npurposes\n\n(1) In performing the function mentioned in paragraph 15(ma), the\nSystem Operator must comply with a direction from, and follow\nthe guidance of, the Data Governance Board.\n\n(2) If rules made for the purposes of subsection 109(7A) require the\nData Governance Board to take steps to ensure that de-identified\ndata and health information disclosed to persons for research or\npublic health purposes is being used only for those purposes, the\nSystem Operator must not take any steps of its own to ensure that\nthe data and information is being used only for those purposes.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not imply that the System Operator has a duty\nto take steps in relation to use of data and information at a time\nwhen there are no rules of the kind mentioned in subsection (2).\n\nAmendments commencing on Proclamation  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018",
      "skos:definition": "Board in relation to data for research or public health\npurposes\n\n(1) In performing the function mentioned in paragraph 15(ma), the\nSystem Operator must comply with a direction from, and follow\nthe guidance of, the Data Governance Board.\n\n(2) If rules made for the purposes of subsection 109(7A) require the\nData Governance Board to take steps to ensure that de-identified\ndata and health information disclosed to persons for research or\npublic health purposes is being used only for those purposes, the\nSystem Operator must not take any steps of its own to ensure that\nthe data and information is being used only for those purposes.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not imply that the System Operator has a duty\nto take steps in relation to use of data and information at a time\nwhen there are no rules of the kind mentioned in subsection (2).\n\nAmendments commencing on Proclamation  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96e-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "210e1151c87e635f916bd0bc019f41ae2a74186e5b5f8ba21ff38e36a5d488a8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-96e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "96E Relationship between System Operator and Data Governance",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "Board in relation to data for research or public health\npurposes\n\n(1) In performing the function mentioned in paragraph 15(ma), the\nSystem Operator must comply with a direction from, and follow\nthe guidance of, the Data Governance Board.\n\n(2) If rules made for the purposes of subsection 109(7A) require the\nData Governance Board to take steps to ensure that de-identified\ndata and health information disclosed to persons for research or\npublic health purposes is being used only for those purposes, the\nSystem Operator must not take any steps of its own to ensure that\nthe data and information is being used only for those purposes.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not imply that the System Operator has a duty\nto take steps in relation to use of data and information at a time\nwhen there are no rules of the kind mentioned in subsection (2).\n\nAmendments commencing on Proclamation  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018"
    },
