    {
      "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "96G Delegation of functions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-96g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Secretary of the Department consents to the Data\nGovernance Board delegating functions to APS employees in the\nDepartment, the Board may delegate any or all of its functions to\nsuch an APS employee.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\n(2) If the chief executive officer (however described) of the data\ncustodian consents to the Board delegating functions to members\nof the staff mentioned in subsection 19(1) of the Australian\nInstitute of Health and Welfare Act 1987, the Board may delegate\nall or any of its functions to such a member of staff.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate must comply with any written directions of the\nBoard.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendments commencing on Proclamation\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018\n\n(4) The delegation continues in force despite a change in the\nmembership of the Board.\n\n(5) The delegation may be varied or revoked by the Board (whether or\nnot there has been a change in the membership of the Board).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Secretary of the Department consents to the Data\nGovernance Board delegating functions to APS employees in the\nDepartment, the Board may delegate any or all of its functions to\nsuch an APS employee.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\n(2) If the chief executive officer (however described) of the data\ncustodian consents to the Board delegating functions to members\nof the staff mentioned in subsection 19(1) of the Australian\nInstitute of Health and Welfare Act 1987, the Board may delegate\nall or any of its functions to such a member of staff.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate must comply with any written directions of the\nBoard.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendments commencing on Proclamation\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018\n\n(4) The delegation continues in force despite a change in the\nmembership of the Board.\n\n(5) The delegation may be varied or revoked by the Board (whether or\nnot there has been a change in the membership of the Board).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96g-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96g-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96g-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-96g-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "34e4007e356bf5a39d52ddf9d1303e876b56538b7708f2b6455e0c2ed6e03bd1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-96g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "96G Delegation of functions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Secretary of the Department consents to the Data\nGovernance Board delegating functions to APS employees in the\nDepartment, the Board may delegate any or all of its functions to\nsuch an APS employee.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\n(2) If the chief executive officer (however described) of the data\ncustodian consents to the Board delegating functions to members\nof the staff mentioned in subsection 19(1) of the Australian\nInstitute of Health and Welfare Act 1987, the Board may delegate\nall or any of its functions to such a member of staff.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate must comply with any written directions of the\nBoard.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendments commencing on Proclamation\n\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\nNo. 154, 2018\n\n(4) The delegation continues in force despite a change in the\nmembership of the Board.\n\n(5) The delegation may be varied or revoked by the Board (whether or\nnot there has been a change in the membership of the Board)."
    },
