          "@id": "concept:my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018-sch-2-sec-109a-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d84c925de228c69cfda19b64862dd74177cfd4f431e9eebf662986222811238d",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of de-identified data or health information is restricted to specific means."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/my-health-records-amendment-strengthening-privacy-act-2018#sch-2-sec-109a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "109A(4) My Health Records Rules relating to data for research or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the rules make provision for the disclosure of de-identified data\nor health information obtained by using or gaining access to the\n\nAmendments commencing on Proclamation  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 154, 2018\nMy Health Records Amendment (Strengthening Privacy) Act 2018\n\nMy Health Record system, the rules must have the effect that the\ndata or information is to be disclosed only:\n\n(a) by means of a postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like\nservice; or\n\n(b) by or to a corporation to which paragraph 51(xx) of the\nConstitution applies; or\n\n(c) by or to a person within a Territory or a place acquired by the\nCommonwealth for a public purpose; or\n\n(d) by or to the Commonwealth or an authority of the\nCommonwealth."
    },
